          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Complex algebraic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surfaces"} K3-surfaces
            admit the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibrations"} elliptic fibrations
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^1
            = succeed "." do
              %em elliptic K3-surfaces
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#SingularPoints Singular points
          %p
            Counted with multiplicity, these elliptic fibrations have 24 singular points (where the
            = succeed "-fiber" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            or
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cuspidal+curve"} cuspidal curve
          %p
            (review in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Huybrechts16"} Huybrechts 16, Section 2-2.4
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "K3-spectrum#Propp18"} Propp 18, p. 4
          %p
            This number 24 of singularities-with-multiplicities is identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+number"} Euler number
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            underlying the (complex analytic)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Shimada00"} Shimada 00, p. 432 (10 of 24)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SchuttShioda09"} Schütt-Shioda 09, Section 6.7, Theorem 6.10
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Huybrechts16"} Huybrechts 16, Chapter 11, Remark 1.12
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Marquart02"} Marquart 02, Section A.3.3, p. 59
          %h3#Classification Classification
          %p
            Up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            of possible such elliptic fibrations.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Nikulin10"}> Nikulin 10
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lecacheux19"} Lecacheux 19
          %h2#in_ftheory In F-theory
          %p
            Elliptically fibered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+manifolds"} Calabi-Yau manifolds
            play a central role in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
          %p
            In passing from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in 11d becomes the locus of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in 10d. The locus of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+monopole"} Kaluza-Klein monopole
            in turn (as discussed there) is the locus where the
            = succeed "-circle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            this is the locus where the fiber of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1_A \times S^1_B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            degenerates to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-dual
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            in F-theory “are” the singular locus of the elliptic fibration.
          %p
            Now an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptically fibered
            complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surface"} K3-surface
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                          %mn 3
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℂ
                          %msup
                            %mi ℙ
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; K3
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{C}\mathbb{P}^1
                  }
          %p
            may be parameterized via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weierstrass+elliptic+function"} Weierstrass elliptic function
            as the solution locus of the equation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  y^2 = x^3 + f(z) x + g(z)
          %p
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z \in \mathbb{C}\mathbb{P}^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            of degree 8 and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            of degree twelve. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            of the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            which this parameterizes for given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 24
                      %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 3
                    %mrow
                      %mn 27
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mn 4
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j(\tau(z)) = \frac{4 (24 f)^3}{27 g^2 + 4 f^3}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poles"} poles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\to \infty
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            correspond to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D7-branes"} D7-branes
            are located.
          %p
            Since the order of the poles is 24 (the polynomial degree of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discriminant"} discriminant
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 27
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mn 4
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta = 27 g^2 + 4 f^3
            %em 24 D7-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "F-theory#Sen96"}> Sen 96, page 5
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "F-theory#Sen97b"} Sen 97b
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "F-theory#Morrison04"} Morrison 04, sections 8 and 17
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "F-theory#Denef08"} Denef 08, around (3.41)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "duality+between+M%2FF-theory+and+heterotic+string+theory#DouglasParkSchnell14"} Douglas-Park-Schnell 14
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            this translates to 24
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            (
            %a{:href => "#Vafa96"}> Vafa 96, Footnote 2 on p. 6
            ).
          %p
            Notice that the
            %em net charge
            of these 24 D7-branes is supposed to vanish, due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            effects (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "F-theory#Denef08"} Denef 08, below (3.41)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F%2FM-theory+on+elliptically+fibered+Calabi-Yau+2-folds"} F-theory on CY2
          %h2#references References
          %p Basics:
          %ul
            %li#FriedmanMorgan94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Friedman"}> Robert Friedman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Smooth Four-Manifolds and Complex Surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783540570585"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-03028-8
            %li#Shimada00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ichiro+Shimada"}> Ichiro Shimada
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On elliptic K3 surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.mmj/1030132587"} euclid:mmj/1030132587
            %li#SchuttShioda09
              %p
                Matthias Schütt, Tetsuji Shioda, Section 12 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elliptic surfaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.0298"} arXiv:0907.0298
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.aspm/1543085637"} euclid:aspm/1543085637
            %li#Huybrechts16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Huybrechts"}> Daniel Huybrechts
                , Chapter 11 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on K3-surfaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/huybrech/K3Global.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HuybrechtsLecturesOnK3.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781316594193"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781316594193
          %p Further review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tristan+H%C3%BCbsch"}> Tristan Hübsch
                , Section 6.2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calabi-Yau Manifolds – A Bestiary for Physicists
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/1410"} doi:10.1142/1410
            %li#Marquart02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monika+Marquart"}> Monika Marquart
                , Section A.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Applications of Dualities in String Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://sundoc.bibliothek.uni-halle.de/diss-online/02/02H150"} sundoc:02/02H150
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://sundoc.bibliothek.uni-halle.de/diss-online/02/02H150/prom.pdf"} pdf
          %p Classification:
          %ul
            %li#Nikulin10
              %p
                Viacheslav Nikulin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elliptic fibrations on K3 surfaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1010.3904"} arXiv:1010.3904
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0013091513000953"} doi:10.1017/S0013091513000953
            %li#Lecacheux19
              %p
                O. Lecacheux,
                %em Weierstrass Equations for the Elliptic Fibrations of a K3 Surface
                In: Balakrishnan J., Folsom A., Lalín M., Manes M. (eds.)
                %em
                  Research Directions in Number Theory Association for Women in Mathematics Series, vol 19. Springer (2019) (
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-19478-9_4"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-030-19478-9_4
                  )
            %li
              %p
                Marie Bertin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elliptic Fibrations on K3 surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~marie-jose.bertin/WINEurope13.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-spectra"} K3-spectra
          %ul
            %li#Propp18
              Oron Y. Propp,
              %em Constructing explicit K3-spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.08953"}> arXiv:1810.08953
              )
